  moves 1.1015 -> 1.1342 = 0.0327 in gamma. The frozen sigma_sys alone is 0.02.

====================================================================================================
S2 -- SENSITIVITY: the 1/4-POWER DESENSITIZATION, d ln a0 / d ln gamma  (analytic+numeric)
====================================================================================================
  Closed form.  gamma = (1 + C/yE)^(1/4),  yE = y_newt(g_ext/a0):
    d ln gamma / d ln yE   = -(1/4) (C/yE) / (1 + C/yE)
    d ln yE   / d ln y_obs = 2 y_obs^2 / (yE sqrt(1+4 y_obs^2)),   y_obs = g_ext/a0
    d ln y_obs/ d ln a0    = -1
  =>  A_log  == d ln a0 / d ln gamma  =  -1 / [ (dlngamma/dlnyE)(dlnyE/dlny_obs) ]
      A_abs  == d ln a0 / d gamma     =  A_log / gamma        (per ABSOLUTE gamma unit)

  footing     g_ext     law     gamma   y_extN    A_log  A_closed    A_abs   meaning
  canonical   primary   MI     1.1015   1.4643    9.726     9.939    8.829   1% in gamma -> 9.7% in a0
  canonical   primary   MG     1.1390   1.4643    7.857     7.857    6.898   1% in gamma -> 7.9% in a0
  canonical   alt-conv  MI     1.0854   1.7757   11.493    11.734   10.589   1% in gamma -> 11.5% in a0
  canonical   alt-conv  MG     1.1182   1.7757    9.103     9.103    8.141   1% in gamma -> 9.1% in a0
  ALT         primary   MI     1.1254   1.1510    7.972     8.152    7.084   1% in gamma -> 8.0% in a0
  ALT         primary   MG     1.1692   1.1510    6.604     6.604    5.648   1% in gamma -> 6.6% in a0
  ALT         alt-conv  MI     1.1053   1.4057    9.396     9.603    8.501   1% in gamma -> 9.4% in a0
  ALT         alt-conv  MG     1.1438   1.4057    7.623     7.623    6.665   1% in gamma -> 7.6% in a0
  [MG rows: closed form == finite difference to 1e-6 (C = 1 identically -> the closed
   form is exact). MI rows differ by 2.2% because the per-star MI
   prescription's effective C drifts weakly with y_extN. The NUMERIC value is used
   everywhere below; for MI it is the SMALLER (more GENEROUS to WB) of the two, so the
   verdict is not helped by this choice.]

  FRAMEWORK-FIRST NUMBER (MI, canonical, primary g_ext): A_log = 9.73, A_abs = 8.83 per unit gamma.
    -> a 1% gamma error is a 9.7% a0 error;  sigma(a0)/a0 = 8.83 x sigma(gamma).
  MG reading is MILDER (7.86) because C=1 > C_MI=0.692 puts the
    asymptote further from 1; the framework's own MI reading is the WORSE case, and
    working-rule 1 says the MI reading is the one that decides.
  WHY: two stacked desensitizations. (i) the 1/4 power; (ii) the EFE saturation --
    a0 enters only inside y_extN, and y_newt() COMPRESSES it (d ln yE/d ln a0 = -1.255, not -1).
  CONTRAST -- the dwarf a0-line: a0 = (g_obs^2 - g_bar^2)/g_bar is a DIRECT amplitude,
    d ln a0 / d ln g_obs = 2 g_obs^2/(g_obs^2-g_bar^2) -> 2 deep; d ln a0/d ln Upsilon
    = -phi(2y+1) -> O(1). Amplification ~1-2, vs WB's ~10. THAT ratio (~5x) is the structural
    reason WB's *smaller percentage* systematics do not buy a smaller a0 error.

====================================================================================================
S3 -- THE C-a0 DEGENERACY (the risk flagged in the brief): does WB constrain a0 or C*a0^p?
====================================================================================================
  Take logs of the committed law:  ln(gamma^4 - 1) = ln C - ln yE(a0).  Therefore
     d ln(gamma^4-1) = d ln C + p d ln a0,     p == -d ln yE/d ln a0 = 1.2545
  A SINGLE measured gamma therefore constrains EXACTLY ONE combination: C * a0^1.255 = const.
  a0 is extractable ONLY if C is known a priori -- i.e. only if the EFE prescription is
  FIXED. It is not: the MI-vs-MG choice is precisely a choice of C.

  DEMONSTRATION -- feed the SAME observed gamma to both prescriptions:
   observed gamma   a0 | MI reading   a0 | MG reading    ratio
           1.0600         5.803e-11         4.153e-11    1.397
           1.0900         8.398e-11         6.159e-11    1.363
           1.1015         9.360e-11         6.921e-11    1.352
           1.1200         1.087e-10         8.129e-11    1.337
           1.1390         1.238e-10         9.360e-11    1.322
           1.1600         1.402e-10         1.071e-10    1.309
  => the prescription ambiguity ALONE moves the extracted a0 by 35.2%  (= 5.6x the 6.31% target),
     with NO measurement error at all. And the framework's MI completion is UNWRITTEN
     (banked: the per-star MI-EFE law is a PRESCRIPTION, not a theorem) -- so C is not
     going to be pinned by theory before DR4.

  RIGOROUS VERSION -- 2-parameter Fisher (ln a0, ln C) on the FROZEN DR4 binning/shape:
    frozen shape gamma(y) = 1 + (Gamma(a0,C)-1) * yE(a0)/(yE(a0)+y),  Gamma=(1+C/yE)^(1/4)
    bins = frozen log10(y) edges; y_b fixed by PHYSICAL g_N (a0-independent binning of
    the sky data), pair counts ~ dN/dlog s from a Opik-like s^-1.5 separation law,
    per-bin sigma calibrated so the 1-PARAMETER (Gamma-only) error reproduces 0.0191.
    calibration: per-bin sigma = 1.845/sqrt(n_b) reproduces sigma(Gamma) = 0.0191 at N=30,000
      log10 y  g_N [m/s^2]  s [kAU]     n_b  sigma_b
        -0.95    1.050e-11    29.11    2574   0.0364
        -0.65    2.095e-11    20.61    2735   0.0353
        -0.35    4.181e-11    14.59    3250   0.0324
        -0.05    8.342e-11    10.33    4080   0.0289
         0.30    1.868e-10     6.90    6039   0.0237
         0.75    5.264e-10     4.11   11322   0.0173

    [MI, C=0.6916]  sigma(ln a0) with C FIXED (conditional) =  18.35%
                     sigma(ln a0) with C FREE  (marginal)    = 365.32%   correlation rho = -0.9987
                     flat direction:  d ln C / d ln a0 = -1.1785  vs the asymptote-only analytic -1.2545
                     (the 6% offset IS the shape's degeneracy-breaking power -- and it is why the
                      marginal error is 20x the conditional one, not infinite)
                     REVERSED (the useful direction): a0 FIXED by the dwarf line ->  sigma(ln C) = 21.62%

    [MG, C=1.0000]  sigma(ln a0) with C FIXED (conditional) =  14.07%
                     sigma(ln a0) with C FREE  (marginal)    = 266.91%   correlation rho = -0.9986
                     flat direction:  d ln C / d ln a0 = -1.1750  vs the asymptote-only analytic -1.2545
                     (the 6% offset IS the shape's degeneracy-breaking power -- and it is why the
                      marginal error is 19x the conditional one, not infinite)
                     REVERSED (the useful direction): a0 FIXED by the dwarf line ->  sigma(ln C) = 16.53%

  READING: with the prescription FREE the marginal sigma(ln a0) EXPLODES (rho = -0.9987, |rho|->1);
  the 8-bin shape does NOT break the degeneracy at any realistic N. The reason is S3b.

  S3b -- WHY THE SHAPE CANNOT BREAK IT: where is the transition, physically?
    In the EFE-saturated regime the boost turns on where the INTERNAL Newtonian field
    drops below the EXTERNAL one, g_N(s) ~ g_extN -- and g_extN = yE(a0)*a0 is almost
    a0-INDEPENDENT because y_newt compresses the ratio. Numerically:
             a0  g_extN = yE*a0  s_half [kAU]  s(g_N=a0) [kAU]
      9.360e-11      1.3706e-10         8.057            9.750
      1.000e-10      1.3470e-10         8.127            9.432
      1.130e-10      1.3006e-10         8.271            8.873
      1.200e-10      1.2765e-10         8.349            8.611
    d ln s_half / d ln a0 = +0.1431  ->  a 1% shift in the measured transition
    location would be a 7.0% a0 measurement -- but the transition location is
    itself only measurable to tens of percent (the boost amplitude is ~0.1 and the
    curve is a shallow single-decade rollover), so this channel is WEAKER than the
    amplitude, not a rescue. And it is degenerate with g_ext, not just with C.
  ==> CONFIRMED, as the frozen pre-registration already states (sec 1.1): 'DR4 gamma_v
      constrains the nu+EFE prescription, NOT the value a0 = 9.36e-11.' This script
      supplies the quantitative version of that frozen sentence.

