  (b) PHOTOMETRIC STELLAR MASS -- CORRECTION OF THE PRIOR OVERSTATEMENT
      WB masses are NOT systematic-free. They come from the Banik+2024 eq.6 cubic
      M_G -> M (Pecaut-Mamajek/FLAME calibrated), per-pair error 5.5% (his sec 2.3.3).
      Propagation: gamma is v_obs / sqrt(G M_tot / s), so gamma ~ M^(-1/2):
         d ln gamma = -0.5 d ln M   ->   d gamma = -0.5 gamma d ln M
      SPLIT (the load-bearing distinction, exactly as in STEP A):
        * per-pair RANDOM 5.5%: AVERAGES DOWN -> 0.016% in gamma at N=30k. Negligible. TRUE 'tighter than Upsilon'.
        * COHERENT ZERO-POINT of the M-L relation: (0.02, 0.035, 0.05) = **ASSUMED BAND** (2-5%).
          Grounds (stated, not hidden): main-sequence M-L calibrations are good to a few
          per cent, BUT the sample-average metallicity/age offset, the Gaia G-band
          bandpass/extinction zero-point, and residual unresolved-faint-companion light
          (which biases photometric M HIGH) are all coherent across the whole catalog.
          This is genuinely TIGHTER than the galaxy Upsilon 0.10 dex (=23%) -- by ~6x --
          and it STILL does not help, because of the amplification (see the a0 column).
          coherent  2.0% mass -> gamma 0.0110 -> a0   9.7%
          coherent  3.5% mass -> gamma 0.0193 -> a0  17.0%
          coherent  5.0% mass -> gamma 0.0275 -> a0  24.3%
      HONEST HEADLINE: galaxy Upsilon 23% x amplification ~1 = ~8% in a0 (STEP A's sysU
      is 8.1%);  WB mass 3.5% x amplification 8.8 = 17.0% in a0. The 6x tighter
      calibration is MORE than undone by the ~9x worse lever. 'No Upsilon at all' is FALSE.

  (c) ECCENTRICITY PRIOR: gate-measured flat-vs-thermal shift = 0.0150 in gamma
      (Hwang+2022 SUPERTHERMAL lies beyond thermal on the same axis, same magnitude,
      opposite sign -> carried symmetric).  -> a0: 13.2%

  (d) DEPROJECTION / ORBITAL-a PRIOR: the committed wb_mond_orbit_mc.py finding is that
      a log-uniform 3D semi-major-axis prior leaks deep-regime apocentre boost into
      high-acceleration sky bins -- Newton-pop returns 0.60-0.67 vtilde vs the validated
