====================================================================================================
VERDICT (honest, both directions -- a manufactured GO and a manufactured NO-GO are equal)
====================================================================================================
  1. THE SENSITIVITY IS THE KILLER, NOT THE SYSTEMATICS LIST. The 1/4 power PLUS EFE
     saturation give d ln a0/d ln gamma = 9.73 (MI, the framework's own
     reading; 7.86 for MG). Per absolute gamma unit, sigma(a0)/a0 = 8.83 sigma(gamma).
     The dwarf a0-line's amplification is ~1-2. WB needs ~6x better fractional
     precision than the dwarf line just to TIE it. It does not have it.
  2. THE DEGENERACY BLOCKS THE AMPLITUDE EXTRACTION OUTRIGHT. A single gamma constrains
     C * a0^1.255 only (exact, S3). With C free the Fisher marginal sigma(ln a0) is
     365% (rho = -0.9987); with C fixed by prescription it is 18.3%.
     Choosing MI vs MG alone slides the extracted a0 by 35.2% = 5.6x the target,
     with zero measurement error -- and the MI completion that would pin C is UNWRITTEN.
     The frozen pre-registration already forbids reporting DR4 gamma as an a0 measurement
     (sec 1.1); this is the quantitative backing for that frozen sentence.
  3. CONTAMINATION IS THE SECOND WALL, ONE-SIDED AND UPWARD. DR3's gamma = 1.205 is
     absorbable by f_triple ~ 0.20 (committed audit); the DR3-today WB a0 error is
     ~151%. WB CANNOT supply a usable a0 amplitude TODAY.
     Its bias direction pushes a0 UP, toward the ALT/MOND cluster -- so a naive WB number
     would look like evidence against the canonical footing purely as an artifact.
  4. THE MASS-SYSTEMATIC OVERSTATEMENT IS CORRECTED. WB photometric masses are ~6x
     tighter than galaxy Upsilon in PERCENT (3.5% coherent vs 23%), and that buys
     NOTHING: 17.0% in a0 vs the dwarf line's 8.1% sysU. 'No Upsilon at all'
     is false; the correct statement is 'a smaller mass error through a much worse lever'.
  5. ORTHOGONALITY IS REAL BUT WORTHLESS HERE. The systematics lists ARE disjoint, so the
     joint is a legitimate quadrature -- but 11.62% (+) 35% = 11.04%: the dwarf floor barely
     moves. Even the most generous reading (prescription and g_ext assumed away, WB at
     24.4%) gives 10.50% -- still above 6.31%.
  6. ANSWER TO THE POSED QUESTION: **NO.** Gaia wide binaries cannot supply an
     a0-AMPLITUDE constraint that helps the Step-A floor -- not today (~151%, contamination-
     limited), and not with DR4 (45-95% across the assumed
     contamination band, with a hard 35% floor from the prescription alone even at
     sigma(gamma)=0). Shortfall factors: 3.2x against the SPARC-alone floor,
     1.4x in the single most generous corner. The blocking reason is NOT the
     orthogonality premise (which HOLDS) but (i) the ~9x desensitization of the 1/4-power
     EFE-saturated map and (ii) the exact C-a0 degeneracy that only a WRITTEN MI
     completion could break. Both are structural, not fixable with more pairs.
  7. WHAT WB IS STILL GOOD FOR (unchanged, and not diminished): the frozen DR4 test of
     the nu+EFE PRESCRIPTION -- Newton vs framework-MI 1.09 is forecast DECIDABLE at
     N >~ 12,200. That is a test of the interpolation+EFE physics, not of a0's value.
     No door is closed here; the a0-amplitude door in WB is simply not open, and the
     dwarf a0-line's external-data path (TRGB + M/L + HI campaign) remains the live one.

